Two more suggestions that probably dont matter to anybody:
(Please look at the concept and not the specific implementation)

GOOD IDEA:

1) Allow priests to create alters to their deity...
     Perhaps limit it to 1 per X exp. points.
     Perhaps let knights do it at 1 per 2X exp. points.



FAIR IDEA:

2) Currently when you create a character, it seems you have a 
     template of base atributes that are dependent of each 
     character class.  Then these attributes are modified a couple
     times with a +1 always matched by a -1.

   Instead of this method, why not allow the player to make these
     modifications.  The people around here tend to just restart until
     they like their character anyways...  (personally I dont care..)

2a)  Along the same lines, with characters like the Wizard, why not
       allow a choice of one or two of their magic items (before knowing
       what the others are).  Again this falls into, the "I will just
       keep rerolling until I get object X anyways..."



